  "warnings": [],
  "working_thesis": "The modern age is defined by world and earth alienation originating from three threshold events—the discovery of America, the Reformation, and the invention of the telescope—leading to the discovery of the Archimedean point, Cartesian doubt, introspection, and the reversal of the hierarchical order of the vita activa where animal laborans and universal science ultimately predominate over contemplation and fabrication."
